    "body": "progress: bherbruck · 2026-11-08T01:07:12Z · fix committed on issue/237-wide-class-bins (fork): inside each wide latitude class the pencil is cut into 0.02-wide latitude bins, and a bin whose 1st-4th bearing harmonic keeps over half its area counts as folded; a pencil whose folded area passes 2% of the inliers does not bear the axis out (the 10% bias budget let the 6x6x80 rod's ~7% through). Pinned by `axis_point::wide_tests`: the 120x60 / 144x72 / 180x90 balls with the 10x10x100 rod, the 6x6x80 rod and the 40x4x100 flat bar never read a cross axis; the tilted copy never reads the tilted cross axis; the ball alone is still refused. All 56 multiaxis unit tests (every #208/#223 pin) pass. Known consequence, fail closed: a square section inside a dome about its true axis is refused too (a hex is not). Full motion + app gate running; PR follows.",
